---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../../site/components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import "../../site/styles/link-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Link study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of secondary links for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="link-study">
    <div class="shell link-study-intro">
      <a class="link-study-back" href="/prototypes/header-study/">← Header study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should a quieter action speak?</h1>
      <p class="link-study-lede">Three ways to handle supporting actions beside the solid-blue button: underline, rule, or a small directional cue.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="shell link-study-grid">
      <article class="link-option">
        <p class="link-option-name"><span>A</span> Underline</p>
        <div class="link-demo"><a class="study-link study-link--underline" href="/transformations/">Browse local transformations <ArrowIcon /></a></div>
        <p>Familiar and explicit. The underline stays visible, so the link reads clearly without relying on hover.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="link-option">
        <p class="link-option-name"><span>B</span> Colour rule</p>
        <div class="link-demo"><a class="study-link study-link--rule" href="/transformations/">Browse local transformations <ArrowIcon /></a></div>
        <p>A yellow rule gives the link a small brand signature while keeping the page quieter than a filled button.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="link-option">
        <p class="link-option-name"><span>C</span> Directional</p>
        <div class="link-demo"><a class="study-link study-link--directional" href="/transformations/">Browse local transformations <ArrowIcon /></a></div>
        <p>Removes the persistent decoration. The arrow and a slight colour shift carry the interaction.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
